{
  "id": "COMPOUND:39010 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-sophorotrioside is implicated in the interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which serves as a target for multiple compounds, including 2,4,6-Trihydroxy-3-(3,3-Dimethylallyl)Acetophenone, 2-amino-3-(1-methyl-1H-imidazol-5-yl)propanoic acid, and Tetracosanoic Acid. All these compounds ultimately target Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting a potential pathway where Kaempferol 3-sophorotrioside may modulate the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn influences Phosphodiesterase 6C. The shared target of these compounds at Phosphodiesterase 6C implies a possible mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-sophorotrioside could exert its effects, possibly through the regulation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence supports a role for this compound in the modulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
